## Why This Is Asked
To assess practical config rotation in Swarm and application reload behavior.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config rotation with versioned configs
- Rolling updates with update-parallelism and update-delay for zero downtime
- Graceful reload semantics (SIGHUP or /reload endpoint)
- Update order start-first to ensure new containers start before old ones stop

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js reload handler
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/flags.json','utf8'));
process.on('SIGHUP', () => {
  flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/flags.json','utf8'));
  // apply flags to runtime features
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the zero-downtime rollout in a CI pipeline?
- What failure scenarios would prompt you to revert the config rotation?
- How would you handle config validation before rotation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to add non-intrusive QA in production, teaches traffic manipulation without risking user impact, and validates multi-DC deployment awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Traffic shadowing vs canary releases
- Nginx mirror and upstream configuration
- Docker-DC/edge proxy routing across DCs
- TLS edge termination and tenant isolation

## Code Example
```nginx
# Example shadow config snippet
upstream prod_api { server prod-api:8080; }
upstream staging_api { server staging-api:8080; }
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://prod_api;
    mirror /mirror_to_staging;
  }
  location = /mirror_to_staging {
    proxy_pass http://staging_api;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor shadowed traffic to ensure no unseen side effects?
- How would you prevent skew if tenant_id headers can be spoofed?
